The equivalence-hash implementations in JsonElementExtensions.cs and
JsonNodeExtensions.cs include code adapted from this Stack Overflow answer:
https://stackoverflow.com/a/60592310/878701
The upstream source identifies that code as CC BY-SA 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
The full license is installed as LICENSE.CC-BY-SA-4.0.

The MSYS2 packaging patch modifies JsonElement numeric hashing so that
decimal-equivalent JSON numbers produce equal hashes. The patch and complete
modified source are available with the source recipe; upstream modifications
are retained in the pinned json-everything source archive.
